I chunk geometry: quantum 16 (attn block 16, state chunk 1), checkpoint interval 4096, max_tok 4096 -> prefill chunks of at most 4096
I prefix resume: exact -- a hit resumes only where an idle server's cold prefill of the same prompt starts a chunk (every 4096 tokens) and a prompt's tail snapshot is taken where its last chunk starts, so the hit recomputes the cold run's own chunks and answers bit-identically; a turn re-prefills up to one chunk more than --prefix-resume nearest
I checkpoint slots: auto: 6 linear-state + sliding-window snapshot(s) of 22.59 MiB in pinned host memory (135.56 MiB), none of it on the card; 6 a sequence for --max-num-seqs 1: geometric-backoff keeps 5 for a 32768-token session at a 4096-token interval, and one more for a running turn
I kv tiers: off (no --prefix-cache-mib); a finished conversation's KV stays in VRAM until the cache evicts it
I prefix cache: 4 paged group(s) in 2-token entries; checkpoints every 4096 tokens (6 slots of 5.65 MiB a rank, pinned host memory), retention 'geometric-backoff'
I end-of-request snapshots: on (RADIANCE_EXPERIMENTAL_PREFIX_EORS) -- a decode step whose row completes a position on the 4096-token resume grid past its prompt snapshots the state there, a prompt ending on the grid snapshots its end and every prompt the start of its last chunk, so a conversation's next turn resumes at most 4095 tokens before the reply's last computed position and recomputes the cold run's own chunks from there; such a step is not issued ahead, and the trim after a publish keeps the entries of the chain just published that the request recomputed rather than adopted
I prefix cache: a trunk layer's windowed group is not prefix-cached -- a hit resumes from a window snapshot (a checkpoint slot)
I end-of-request snapshots: on a 16-token grid (RADIANCE_EXPERIMENTAL_DS41_RESUME_GRID) -- a decode step whose row completes a multiple of 16 past its prompt snapshots the state there, and a prompt ending on one its end, so the next turn resumes at most 15 tokens below the reply's last computed position, off the 4096-token chunk grid, and prefills from there in chunks of its own up to the next interval boundary or tail and the cold run's after; exact by DeepSeek-V4.1's partition invariance under large-chunk prefill (a row's bits do not depend on the pass that computes it); such a step is not issued ahead
